# {{title}}: design agent instructions

This folder is a self-contained design workspace for the **{{title}}** prototype of
**{{projectName}}**. It is meant to be imported on its own into Claude Design, or opened by any
design agent. You do not need the rest of the repository; everything the design depends on is here.

Your job is to turn the agreed structure in `context/` into interactive prototypes that the
project's coding agent can implement without guessing.

## Read first

1. `context/brief.md`: the problem, audience, outcome and agreed scope.
2. `context/screens.md`: every screen with its stable ID, route, components and interactions.
3. `context/components.md`: the shared component inventory and where each component is used.
4. `context/design-tokens.md`: the platform, its visual tokens and the constraints of the frontend.
5. `context/project.json`: the canonical design model. It is the machine source of the files above.
   Read it; never edit it.

